Shawn I Roske wrote:
>
> so i start a new game, rng gives me a scroll of punishment and a scroll
> of remove curse.  i figure to experiment and discover what remove curse
> does to the ol' ball and chain.  Lo!  it leaves the iron ball!  it makes
> quite a weapon.  too bad my wizard was burdened carrying it.  what do
> you think about using this as a strategy for the early game.  is the
> iron ball a good weapon, maybe for a warrior type?

An iron ball does d25 damage which is better than any non-artifact
non-enchanted weapon.  Any good artifact will beat it.  Any good
regular weapon that's maybe +3 or higher will beat it.  As such it
is okay early on but never to be gotten deliberately.

An iron ball weighs 480.  That's *4* times as much as a dwarvish
mattock (arguably the best early weapon until you get something
to highly enchant) and *48* times as much as a dagger.

Consider how much damage you could do machine gunning
with a quiver filled with 48 uncursed +0 regular daggers.  It's far
more than an iron ball.  As such if you're stuck with an iron ball
go ahead and use it but never chose to get one.



